  "id": "involuntary-treatment",
  "term": "involuntary treatment",
  "definition": "Involuntary treatment is care given without a patient's agreement, used in this context when anorexia nervosa is judged to create serious risk to the person or others, and in some places to stop further worsening. It is described as a controversial practice because its use, timing, and effects are complex for both patients and clinicians.",
